the northernmost stretch of thailand's  border with myanmar  is a natural one the doi nangnong  mountain range  while the landscape might be beautiful  it makes it difficult for thai army  patrols to search for migrants crossing  illegally  with concern growing over myanmar's  increase in covid19 cases  those patrols have grown bigger and more  frequent  this says the number of migrants  attempting to cross has surged over the  last several weeks  thailand has been much more successful  in controlling covid19  and has better healthcare the thai  border areas are on high alert many of  the crossings take place at night  making it easier to avoid being caught  but also increasing the danger  one of those migrants who risked the  night crossing a mother of two  in thailand illegally were hiding her  face  ann used to sort avocados on the thai  side of the border but in may she  sneaked back into myanmar to see her  mother before she died  she returned to her house a few weeks  ago it's been tense with her thai  neighbors since  she says they treat her like a disease  and informed local authorities  that she returned  everybody is scared of it but it was  absolutely necessary for us to come back  i was prepared to notify the local  health volunteers and the head of the  village  it was along this stretch of the sci  river that serves as the border  that anne and her daughter snuck back  into thailand because  of monsoonal rains it was swollen and  fast moving her daughter  had to ride on the shoulders of someone  who was crossing at the same time  it's not just anne's neighborhood one  group that works with migrants is also  seeing cases of locals alerting  authorities  about people who've crossed illegally  if they come into the community after  illegally crossing and people see them  they will notify immigration they don't  care  there's only a trickle of cargo passing  through the usually bustling masai  border post  since the rapid spread in myanmar more  precautions have been put in place at  the official crossing  we coordinate with the department of  disease control to intensify the  checking of cargo vehicles  and their drivers but as the situation  worsens in myanmar people seeking safety  and better health care  will continue to take the risk and cross  over any way they can  scott hiller al jazeera masai thailand
 

